{"name": "berserk-c82-p01", "created": 1789574867.155094, "updated": 1789575026.0299819, "params": {"n_predict": 60, "stop": [], "temperature": 2.5, "min_p": 0.08, "top_k": 0, "top_p": 1.0, "top_n_sigma": -1, "xtc_probability": 0.5, "xtc_threshold": 0.1, "repeat_penalty": 1.05, "repeat_last_n": 512, "dry_multiplier": 0.8, "dry_base": 1.75, "dry_allowed_length": 3, "dry_penalty_last_n": 8192, "ignore_eos": false, "n_probs": 5, "logit_bias": [], "logit_bias_text": "", "fan": 4, "spread": 1.0, "dry_keep": 0.8}, "turn": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "root": "56251449", "current": "a93e4feb", "nodes": {"56251449": {"id": "56251449", "parent": null, "kind": "root", "text": "Municipal Lifts Office\nAcceptance tests following the removal of a floor\n\nBuilding 6, North Court. The fourth floor was removed on 11 March. Its button has been blanked. No alteration to the numbering of the floors above is authorised.\n\nTest 1. Empty car sent from third to fifth. Passed without stopping.\nTest 2. Car loaded with sacks to the weight of one adult. Passed without stopping.\nTest 3. Same load, with a hat placed on the upper sack. Stopped between third and fifth. Doors remained closed for the regulation interval.\n\nThe inspector repeated Test 3 without the hat. This time\n", "ts": 1789574867.155093, "pruned": false, "posed": false, "meta": null}, "bb2c8b43": {"id": "bb2c8b43", "parent": "56251449", "kind": "human", "text": "\n\ni keep coming back to one line of it.\n", "ts": 1789574867.155521, "pruned": false, "posed": true, "meta": null}, "be6be798": {"id": "be6be798", "parent": "bb2c8b43", "kind": "model", "text": "Stopped between third and fifth.\n\n\nthe phrase makes me laugh each time I read it but there are no jokes in it.\n\nwhat i see when i read it:  a person stops between two floors. this could mean any number of things and i think about all the different possibilities that i can come", "ts": 1789574872.930061, "pruned": false, "posed": false, "meta": {"stop_type": "limit", 